  "findings": [
    "A fixed tolerance (1e-6 x max eigenvalue) on DE results missed 4 of 12 degenerate runs; the gap ratio w_min/w_next < 1e-3 detected all 12 and rejected all 6 controls; after a classical L-BFGS-B polish the fixed tolerance also detected all 12.",
    "The polish changed E_cl by at most about 1e-11 and reduced the axis error from about 1e-5 to about 1e-7.",
    "The tilted-field control has gap ratio 2e-2 against at most 5e-5 for degenerate DE runs; weaker classical pinning would narrow this margin, so the ratio should be recorded, not only the verdict.",
    "For the polarized control the vanishing z generator has relative singular value 3-8e-6 from DE and 2-4e-8 after polish, so the generator-rank tolerance must follow the state accuracy (1e-4 used here).",
    "The sixfold E_qm amplitude from the EnergyFunction route agrees with the converged lambda_6 of the independent vacuum_energy route: within 1.1% at N=6 and 0.2% at N=12 for J_PD, within 0.05% at N=6 for J_Gamma.",
    "The minimum is at phi = 0 (mod pi/3) for every case and every N >= 3, within 7.5e-5 rad.",
    "Correction to state-selection-2026-09-29.json: the J_Gamma = 0.010 spread 3.2e-12 is a converged selection (2 lambda_6 with lambda_6 = 1.64e-12), not an unreliable one. A 24-point grid only limits the resolution of its location; a harmonic fit resolves it."
  ],
